---
title: Badge & tag
description: A badge states something — a status, a count. A tag goes somewhere — it is a link to a topic.
eyebrow: Component
source: src/components/badge.css · tag.css
---
<h2>Badge</h2>
{{#example center=true}}
<span class="im-badge">Neutral</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-accent">Accent</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-success">Live</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-warning">Draft</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-danger">Failed</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-info">Guide</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-outline">Outline</span>
{{/example}}

{{#example center=true title="With an icon, and as a pill"}}
<span class="im-badge im-badge-success">{{> "icons/check"}} Published</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-outline">{{> "icons/lock"}} Members</span>
<span class="im-badge im-badge-accent im-badge-pill">{{> "icons/flame"}} Featured</span>
{{/example}}

{{#example title="Beside a heading"}}
<h3 class="flex items-center gap-2.5">Release notes <span class="im-badge im-badge-info">v0.2</span></h3>
{{/example}}

<h2>Tag</h2>
{{#example center=true}}
<a class="im-tag" href="#tag">Travel</a>
<a class="im-tag" href="#tag" aria-current="page">Craft</a>
<a class="im-tag im-tag-dot" href="#tag" style="--im-tag-dot: #0b6e4f">Career</a>
<a class="im-tag im-tag-dot" href="#tag" style="--im-tag-dot: #175cd3">Salesforce</a>
{{/example}}
<p>In Ghost, a tag's own colour is <code>accent_color</code>: <code>style="--im-tag-dot: \{{accent_color}}"</code>. The current tag is <code>aria-current="page"</code>.</p>
